-- title:
--   Orthonormal matrix coordinates preserve all totalized real operator powers
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space, let $b$ be an orthonormal basis, let $X\ge0$, and let $t\in\mathbb R$. If $[X]_b$ is the matrix of $X$, then
--   $$ [X^t]_b=([X]_b)^t. $$
--   No invertibility or sign restriction on $t$ is assumed. Both functional-calculus powers use $0^t=0$ for $t\ne0$ and $0^0=1$. This is full coordinate compatibility of real powers on a finite nonnegative spectrum.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/ComplexTraceHolder.lean#L46-L63

